-- title:
--   Γ-stability of uniformised periods with R-level structure
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N, q, q'$ with $N$ nonzero and $q, q'$ prime, and assume $q \nmid N$, $q' \nmid N$ and $q' \neq q$. Let $a, b \in \mathbb{Q}$ and suppose `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q q'` holds for $B = \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}, a, b]$, i.e. $0 < a$ or $0 < b$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}$ the completed algebra $B \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ has all nonzero elements invertible precisely when $v$ contains $q$ or $q'$. Let $\Lambda \subseteq B$ be a maximal order, i.e. a finitely generated $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule containing $1$, closed under multiplication, spanning $B$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and maximal among such; let $N$ be squarefree and $R \subseteq \Lambda$ an Eichler order of level $N$, i.e. $R = \Lambda_1 \cap \Lambda_2$ for maximal orders $\Lambda_1, \Lambda_2$ with $R$ of relative index $N$ in $\Lambda_1$ as additive subgroups. Let $\iota : B \to M_2(\mathbb{R})$ be an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map. Write $\mathrm{per}_\tau(x) = (\iota x)_{\mathbb{C}} \cdot {}^{t}(\tau, 1)$ for the period map `qmPeriodMap ι τ` and $L_\tau(\Lambda) = \mathrm{per}_\tau(\Lambda)$ for `qmPeriodLattice ι Λ τ`. Let $L, M$ be $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules of $\mathbb{C}^2$, $\tau$ a point of the upper half-plane, and $c \in \mathbb{C}$, $c \neq 0$, with $c \cdot L = L_\tau(\Lambda)$ and with the level condition that for all $\lambda \in \Lambda$ and $r \in R$, $N^{-1}\mathrm{per}_\tau(\lambda) \in c \cdot M$ implies $N^{-1}\mathrm{per}_\tau(\lambda r) \in c \cdot M$. Let $\gamma \in GL_2(\mathbb{R})$ lie in `fuchsianGroup R ι`, that is, $\gamma$ has determinant $1$ and is the image under $\iota$ of an element of the subgroup of $B^{\times}$ generated by the units $u$ satisfying the predicate `IsUnitOf R`. Then there exists $c' \in \mathbb{C}$, $c' \neq 0$, with $c' \cdot L = L_{\gamma \tau}(\Lambda)$ and such that for all $\lambda \in \Lambda$ and $r \in R$, $N^{-1}\mathrm{per}_{\gamma\tau}(\lambda) \in c' \cdot M$ implies $N^{-1}\mathrm{per}_{\gamma\tau}(\lambda r) \in c' \cdot M$.
--
--   This is the $\Gamma$-invariance of the condition that a pair of lattices $(L, M)$ uniformises the period lattice of $\Lambda$ at $\tau$ together with an $R$-stable level-$N$ structure: the condition at $\tau$ transports to $\gamma\tau$ for $\gamma$ in the norm-one Eichler group acting on the upper half-plane. It is used in the analysis of the Shimura curve attached to the indefinite quaternion algebra ramified exactly at $q$ and $q'$, in particular in the open and closed parts of the study of the image of the period construction and of algebraic families of such data.
